From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:29:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] iphlpapi: the Pf* packet filtering API fails as on Windows Vista and later; ICMPv6 echo

Microsoft documents every Pf* function as available only on Windows 2000 and
Server 2003 and returning ERROR_CALL_NOT_SUPPORTED from "Longhorn" on, so the sixteen
exports (PfCreateInterface ... PfDeleteLog) return that error (120) and keep and enforce
nothing; PfAddFiltersToInterface with no filters at all returns the documented
PFERROR_NO_FILTERS_GIVEN first. No firewall rule is touched (DECISIONS item 10).

Icmp6CreateFile, Icmp6SendEcho2 and Icmp6ParseReplies send a real ICMPv6 echo through nsiproxy's
unix side (raw or ping socket, hop limit, source bind, error replies mapped to IP_* statuses).

